{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#4143","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#4143","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#4143\",\"parent_revision\":\"9272f631ba5b01c7c9b4e240a3ea14730e6524733b3c7dd4406b77a17ead5ea4\",\"root_revision\":\"9272f631ba5b01c7c9b4e240a3ea14730e6524733b3c7dd4406b77a17ead5ea4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-10-17\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-10-17T07:20:15.257620Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: dispatch spawn could enqueue work to an itsaplan runner instead of a local spawn process\\nDate: 2026-10-17\\nGoal: Establish planning-ready, evidence-backed requirements for an optional external queued-run dispatch route without assuming infrastructure or authority.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current development-harness local dispatch lifecycle, identity, worktree/branch inputs, and completion evidence are known. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Itsaplan external runner claim, lease, heartbeat, result, failure, retry, and runner-timeout behavior are known from primary source. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. A supported upstream way to cause a specific external-agent queued run with a development-harness dispatch item is established. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. The authoritative mapping between a development-harness wave/item and Itsaplan project, issue, agent, and run identity is decided. | Status: MISSING\\n5. The operator who owns the instance, agent key, MCP enablement, runner machine, and coding-agent authentication is identified. | Status: MISSING\\n6. The permitted unattended permission posture and repository/worktree boundary for external execution are decided. | Status: MISSING\\n7. Whether #4142 is required before #4143 is established. | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 3\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n</div>\\n\\n## Offers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nresearch/task-management/itsaplan.md, \\\"Key Features > AI agents\\\": an external agent runs on the operator's machine through `@itsaplan/runner`, invoked with `npx -y @itsaplan/runner` (entry, Installation & Usage). The runner \\\"polls the instance per agent key\\\" and \\\"gives each queued task to a coding agent CLI\\\" (packages/runner/README.md, as quoted in the entry). Its presets include `claude`, `codex`, and `copilot`. A task's result is read from the exit code: \\\"`0` is a success, and any other code is a failure\\\" (entry, Technical Architecture, Execution model). Queued runs start \\\"on an @mention in a comment, on an assignment, or on a schedule\\\" (entry, Problem Addressed). The REST API is documented in the same entry (see the sibling issue on the backlog backend).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Could Change\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`dispatch spawn` could place each work item as a queued run through the itsaplan REST API, and an `@itsaplan/runner` process on the operator's machine would execute it, in place of a direct `uv run spawn.py` child process. Setup cost: a running itsaplan instance, an agent key per runner, a runner process per machine, and a change to `_build_spawn_cmd`'s caller. The entry documents that the presets pass unattended-run flags: \\\"Claude Code receives `--permission-mode auto`\\\" (entry, AI agents). That changes the permission model for dispatched work, and the change would need its own review before adoption.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Touches\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe dh dispatch path. `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py:1789` sets `_SPAWN_SCRIPT` to `skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py`. `_build_spawn_cmd` at `dh_core/operations.py:1802-1824` builds `[\\\"uv\\\", \\\"run\\\", spawn.py, \\\"--model\\\", model, \\\"--name\\\", \\\"dispatch-{milestone}-{issue_num}\\\"]`, adds `--worktree` for the work phase and `--branch` for the integration branch, and appends `Work on issue #{issue_num}: {item_title}` as the task text.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Read: `research/task-management/itsaplan.md` lines 47-55 (AI agents list) and 84-86 (Execution model for external agents).\\n- Read: `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` lines 1785-1824.\\n- Grep `_SPAWN_SCRIPT|_build_spawn_cmd|spawn.py` in `plugins/development-harness`: confirmed the spawn call site named above.\\n- GitHub issue search `repo:Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills dispatch spawn runner agent`: no issue covering a queued-run or external-runner dispatch path was returned.\\n- Semantic search tools (ccc, graphify) were not run in this scan. Grep and Glob were the search tools used.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dde068fd349f5f25e5553481422229231f09b04908bacb8ba57d683eaf583a13\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABc2evwg\",\"fields\":{\"added\":\"2026-10-17\",\"status\":\"needs-grooming\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"stack\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"source\":\"Not specified\",\"topic\":\"\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"2026-10-17\",\"plan\":\"\",\"files\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"item_type\":\"Feature\"}}"}